{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502581-how-common-is-barter-anong-garou-and-kin","id":1502581,"title":"how common is barter anong garou and kin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-08T20:58:52-08:00","id":1502581,"title":"how common is barter anong garou and kin?","content":"thoughts on craft products like home brewed beer or cheese? <br /> <br /> <br /> or think it could be used to bargain for the uuse of numina","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T21:46:37-08:00","id":1502585,"title":"","content":"I would think it is very common. I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;use of numina&quot;, but trade goods have some kind of value. In close knit communities, the trading of favors or home made goods (farm products, home gardens, handmade crafts, personal services) can be common. As long as people have something others find valuable, avoiding monetary transactions can preserve cash, lower taxes, and build social bonds.<br /> <br /> Garou are supposed to trade Talens as a form of low grade currency so there is definitely a culture of barter. Glass Walkers probably have a more modern mindset based on cash and monetary exchange, but I expect most other tribes have kinfolk that utilize a lot of exchange of goods and services where it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T23:05:15-08:00","id":1502590,"title":"","content":"So this might be a bit afield if your original question PotN, but I do think that it\u2019s connected.<br /> <br /> I think that one reason why barter would definitely be common in the Nation is that, aside from many traditional Garou not having any direct need for money, it serves as one of the major supports for one half of the garou economy - what I\u2019ll call the craft economy (as opposed to the war or loot economy). One of the bases of the craft economy is naturally going to be how many talens and fetishes the theurges are able to produce and how they\u2019re distributed; the theurges become one of the economic engines of the Nation as they can produce what everyone wants (with the spiritual sanction of auspice) and so the things they produce can be used as motivation for every other Garou who wants talens and fetishes to go around doing the things that the theurges (and those they trade with) want done. Of course there is also the trade in favors/services as well as other goods, but I mention fetishes and talens in particular as I imagine they\u2019re a priority for most Garou.<br /> <br /> The reason that I make the Craft and Loot Economy distinction however, is that I also want to talk about the Loot Economy as the other leg of Garou economics. This was inspired by rereading the first two chapters of the Iliad, which I highly recommend as inspirational material for Garou tradition, in particular the idea of \u2018The First Share of the Kill to the Greatest in Station\u2019. Agamemnon helps me see how that works on the economic scale. Let\u2019s say that Sept A has just finished raiding Sept B, at which point they carry off a bunch of fetishes and talens as loot. The Elder of Sept A then claims the loot, may keep the choicest bits for themselves, then distribute the rest to those who participated enough to be worthy of recognition (and bear in mind that if you stiff a Garou on their share of the loot, they\u2019re not gonna be inclined to answer your war-howl anytime soon). This, the loot economy, I see as serving as one of the core pillars of the Garou economy - this is how the elders get the Nation together to take particular courses of action and this is how the Garou elders maintain influence: they distribute the booty.<br /> <br /> One of the other reasons I bring this up is because I think that the Elder-Centrism of the Loot Economy is somewhat different than the Craft Economy, for the simple reason that I don\u2019t think that the average Elder could simply take what any local Theurge produced without it coming off as tyrannical (which isn\u2019t to say that they can\u2019t do it - it simply means that the litany is less clear on the matter then in cases of the war economy and you\u2019re gonna piss off that Theurge at minimum). Which isn\u2019t to say that the Craft Economy wouldn\u2019t be heavily influenced by the elders - after all its elder philodox who mediate disputes and elder theurges who produce the highest quality crafts. <br /> <br /> I know some people will disagree with my points about the Craft Economy, and argue that Elders (and strong Garou in general) can simply challenge for possession of any fetish they want, whether or not the crafts-wolf likes it. I don\u2019t actually disagree with this either in theory, and I fully believe that there would be septs run this way. What I\u2019m arguing is that it shouldn\u2019t be universal, but an expression of local sept culture. If crafters and the Garou they barter with are always going to be steamrolled by their elders, those same Garou may well decide to take drastic actions such as: stop producing crafts, leave the sept, conspire against the elders. The actions which it would take to prevent them from doing so would almost certainly just escalate the tensions in the long run until they boiled over, even in the tribes that would be most ideologically accommodating to the notion such as the Get of Fenris or Shadow Lords. I think that many or most septs, unless you wish to present a Nation on the precipice of mass desertion and revolt, would allow the Craft Economy to be carried out without anymore then the occasional challenge over possession and even then when the elders involved feel that they can justify the action well enough to mollify the bruised egos and suspicion of less renowned garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T01:23:05-08:00","id":1502595,"title":"","content":"I would only disagree on the idea that this is really happening on a scale large enough to really be an economy. I think Black Fox's comparison to what's true for many people as it is: simple barter between members of close knit communities. In the past of the Garou Nation things might have gotten to economic levels (it's not like Sept raiding is considered common practice in modern times, when it clearly was a few generations ago).<br /> <br /> While various historical raiding cultures are worth examining on things like how loot operates to benefit the highest of station while still requiring deft leadership to ensure loyalty among the ranks, Garou having a large focus on loot is a bit iffy because the most valuable thing at a Sept isn't its stockpile of spirit-items: it's the Caern itself. Garou are portrayed as conquerors over raiders in their approach because if you defeat a Sept and take away everything they have to defend their Caern, and then leave, you've breached the Litany. Loot is still part of wars of conquest of course, but so are prestige and status awards that would go into things like who gets to run the new Sept they're going to build to care for their new Caern, and how warleaders are going to shore up defenses until the Sept can stand average attacks on their own.<br /> <br /> While not something most people want to play in their games, Garou pillaging is also going to involve a lot of kin-stealing. Choice kin are, in many ways, more valuable than a Fetish that any of the Theurges already in your command structure could make with some time. Forcing kin to marry into new Garou families is one of the few ways to quickly expand kin and thus Garou numbers. This is also another thing that modern nights have forced the Garou to stop doing because there is simply too much else they need to deal with than this sort of warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T07:08:03-08:00","id":1502602,"title":"","content":"by use of numina I meant compounding a poultice performing a divination etc<br /> <br /> <br /> oh is a arranged marriage aa valid chip on the table","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T14:40:23-08:00","id":1502644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502581-how-common-is-barter-anong-garou-and-kin?p=1502602#post1502602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh is a arranged marriage aa valid chip on the table</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be. While arranged marriages are now uncommon in the West, it was very common historically especially in regards to dynastic marriages, preserving family wealth and power, etc. And it is still practiced in many parts of the world. I imagine the Garou &quot;leaders&quot; of the Garou/kinfolk families practice it often. Probably more historically than today, but the practice is likely widespread.<br /> <br /> Of course this will also be influenced by the typical differences in tribal and sept cultures. The Silver Fangs likely practice it heavily. The Bone Gnawers probably not at all. The Glass Walkers might be too modern to practice it much. Children of Gaia will be reluctant to compel anyone to marry someone they don't. Black Furies might refuse to do it if the female doesn't want it, but may not care about the opinion of the male.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:03:53-08:00","id":1502646,"title":"","content":"I would add the Shadow Lords and some of the Glass Walker Camps as likely to still heavily practice arranged marriages.<br /> <br /> That said, it's worth considering a separation between arranged political marriages that people normally think about, and matchmaking culture where courtship is heavily overseen by a trusted community member. Matchmaking tends to operate in a middle ground between the pure family politics of arranged marriages, and individual initiated love marriage culture. I would expect matchmaking to be very common among the majority of Tribes instead of formal arranged marriages, or leaving everything up to normal human/wolf courtship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T17:22:45-08:00","id":1502661,"title":"","content":"ideas on a good dice roll to use to get a kinfolk especially ones with a modern upbringing to assent to an arranged marriage???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T19:01:23-08:00","id":1502663,"title":"","content":"Social stuff in the WoD is hard to pin down for that. You basically have to balance your best dice-pool with the best approach for addressing the kin's mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T19:08:16-08:00","id":1502664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502581-how-common-is-barter-anong-garou-and-kin?p=1502661#post1502661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ideas on a good dice roll to use to get a kinfolk especially ones with a modern upbringing to assent to an arranged marriage???</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically covered on WoD: Blood and Silk, pages 110-111. Generally, it boils down to Intelligence + Knowledge Ability to find a good prospect (for Garou, that may involve Rituals) and Perception + Empathy to gauge compatibility. Theurges might also be used in place of standard human ritualists to determine omens, which probably uses Enigmas instead of Portents. Misrepresentation of a potential spouse's qualities involves (appropriate Attribute) + Subterfuge, opposed by Perception + Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> (Standard disclaimer for looking at Blood and Silk, do not believe anything written in the &quot;Language and Transliteration&quot; text box on page 8 other than that the PRC uses Pinyin for transliteration. Everything else is pretty terribly wrong. Yes, enough so that I'm taking the time to write this even after supplying the systems. That's what you get for messing up and indirectly claiming that Yale Romanization existed over three hundred years before it was actually created.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T20:31:37-08:00","id":1502672,"title":"","content":"yes but how do I handle persuading kin to assent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T22:38:56-08:00","id":1502676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502581-how-common-is-barter-anong-garou-and-kin?p=1502672#post1502672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes but how do I handle persuading kin to assent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's covered in the social rules in the core book, most likely. Alternately, by making concessions to the kin in a manner not unlike how Dragon-Blooded deal with this sort of thing in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T00:11:15-08:00","id":1502677,"title":"","content":"Ultimately if you want to use systems, you need to establish individual context.<br /> <br /> To go with something different:<br /> <br /> How do you get someone to give you $1,000?<br /> <br /> What systems to break out relies on a lot of things. What's your approach? Are you trying to scare them into it with Intimidation? Con them out of it with Subterfuge? Convince them that it's for the best (also Subterfuge funnily enough) based on getting them to believe you're assessment of the situation? Make an impassioned appeal to their duty and better nature with Expression?<br /> <br /> What's the time table here? Do you need that cash in your hands yesterday? Can you wait a week? A month?<br /> <br /> Are you in a country with easy access to US dollars and have to take into account the potential of needing to find an exchange even if the deal is on?<br /> <br /> And of course, there's their side of it. $1K could be a huge thing to ask of someone that's working minimum wage and only has $200 in the bank. Someone better off but not doing great might be able to cough up the money most of the time, but around the 1st of the month they have a bunch of big bills to cover and aren't going to have a lot of cash around until their next paycheck. And of course they could be filthy rich and the only reason the don't carry that around as pocket change is the physical awkwardness of it.<br /> <br /> Is this a close friend that wants to help you out the best they can? A stranger that has no idea why you're asking them? Someone with a nasty reputation you need to be careful with?<br /> <br /> These things can completely shift the mechanics to use, and why we can't just point to a specific roll in the books.<br /> <br /> There's no one system for this, because you want different thins for handling a Silver Fang kin that was just going with the flow but when the wedding preparations finally start in earnest gets severe cold feet, compared to a Shadow Lord kin that's realized that their parents, and their betrothed's parents, are all getting something out of this, and isn't assenting until some negotiations to haggle of what their cut of the deal is going to be.<br /> <br /> The only important thing to remember is that the Garou do have a pretty solid array of supernatural leverage points to aid their case. There's low hanging fruit like the Persuasion Gift, but also the ability to contact multiple ancestor-spirits for a group peer pressure session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T02:17:44-08:00","id":1502680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502581-how-common-is-barter-anong-garou-and-kin?p=1502672#post1502672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes but how do I handle persuading kin to assent.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you persuade your family, friends or coworkers to help you out or agree in real life? How do indian families still manage to get their kids who are living halfway around the world from them to still do this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai",